  "labelNotes": "Columns checked with pdftotext -layout. Supply: ROC VCCA and VCCB rows are both 1.65-5.5 V; as identical (value, unit, qualifier, conditions) they are labelled once (cited at the VCCA line; 'VCCA' also occurs elsewhere on page 4). Supply currents: VCCA/VCCB columns are not allowed condition keys and 'IO = 0' has no unit, so all ICC rows carry no conditions and collapse: ICCA/ICCB 3 uA MAX (both 1.65-5.5V), 2 uA MAX and -2 uA MAX (the printed negative MAX for the unpowered-side rows, kept as printed), ICCA+ICCB 4 uA MAX, and Delta-ICCA (A port, DIR) / Delta-ICCB 50 uA MAX, each once. Input leakage: only II (DIR control input), printed '\u00b11' (TA = 25 C) and '\u00b12' (TA = -40 to +85 C) in the MAX column, labelled as magnitudes 1 and 2 uA MAX; those value lines are textually identical to the Ioff/IOZ value lines, so citations are not unique. Ioff (power-off I/O leakage) and IOZ (output leakage) excluded. Abs max: VCCA/VCCB supply 6.5 V and VI 6.5 V collapse to one label; VO rows are outputs, skipped."
